    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="1064" n="1854" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v01p2/pg1854"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Eisenhower papers, Whitman
                    file</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Attorney General (Brownell) to the President</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-28">May 28, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This refers to your recent memorandum on the Bricker Amendment.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d368-f1"/> At a conference with the Vice President and the Secretary
                    of State today, the Vice President stated that he would talk to Senator Ferguson
                    about the proposal to reconsider the Bricker Amendment. All three of us believe
                    it would be unfortunate to have the Administration appear to re-open the
                    controversy, and believe that if the matter is re-opened it might well lead to a
                    long filibuster-type debate in the Senate, which would jeopardize the passage of
                    many important Administration measures. This, of course, may be “counsel of
                    perfection” and I realize that there are many factors involved.</p>
                <pb facs="1065" n="1855" xml:id="pg1855"/>
                <p>In the meantime I am studying the legal aspects of the draft of the suggested
                    amendment which you attached to your memorandum, with a view to giving you an
                    answer as soon as possible.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d368-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed>H.B.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d368-f1" n="1" xml:id="d368-f1-content">
                <p>The President’s memorandum of May 26 to Secretary Dulles and Attorney General
                    Brownell, <ref target="#pg1852">p. 1852</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d368-f2" n="2" xml:id="d368-f2-content">
                <p>No record of a further reply by the Attorney General on this matter has been
                    found in Department of State files or at the Eisenhower Library.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
